midterms-ai-stocks: credits and licences

Picture: original code (three.js, MIT licence, https://threejs.org) rendered frame by frame in headless Chromium on this machine. Engine (renderer, bloom, grade, glow points, light trails, labels) reused from film 12 "one-question". No stock footage, no generated video, no paid services, no logos, no candidate likenesses.
Map data: Natural Earth (public domain, https://www.naturalearthdata.com), ne_50m_admin_1_states_provinces via github.com/nvkelso/natural-earth-vector, reprojected to Albers equal-area and simplified by tools/mkus.py (Alaska and Hawaii as insets).
Capitol: simple geometric silhouette built from boxes, cylinders and a half-sphere (no photo, no reference image).
Stock charts: daily closes as reported by the outlets listed in FACTS.md; lines join the closes, with no invented intraday movement.

